1
00:00:00,238 --> 00:00:01,138
Here's a puzzle.

2
00:00:01,138 --> 00:00:02,750
Dolphins are mammals

3
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:04,450
so they need air to breathe.

4
00:00:04,450 --> 00:00:06,212
But they live in the ocean.

5
00:00:06,212 --> 00:00:07,800
So how do they sleep

6
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:08,750
without drowning?

7
00:00:09,649 --> 00:00:11,562
Humans breathe automatically.

8
00:00:11,562 --> 00:00:12,999
You never have to think

9
00:00:12,999 --> 00:00:13,737
about it.

10
00:00:13,737 --> 00:00:16,162
A dolphin's breath is voluntary.

11
00:00:16,162 --> 00:00:17,762
Every single breath

12
00:00:17,762 --> 00:00:19,161
is a conscious decision.

13
00:00:19,161 --> 00:00:20,999
Fall completely asleep

14
00:00:20,999 --> 00:00:22,949
and a dolphin would stop breathing.

15
00:00:23,849 --> 00:00:25,212
So dolphins evolved

16
00:00:25,212 --> 00:00:26,474
a clever workaround.

17
00:00:26,474 --> 00:00:28,211
They sleep with only half

18
00:00:28,211 --> 00:00:29,574
of their brain at a time.

19
00:00:29,574 --> 00:00:31,599
The other half stays awake.

20
00:00:31,599 --> 00:00:33,274
Scientists call it

21
00:00:33,274 --> 00:00:35,349
unihemispheric slow-wave sleep.

22
00:00:36,262 --> 00:00:37,737
The sleeping half rests

23
00:00:37,737 --> 00:00:38,949
while the awake half

24
00:00:38,949 --> 00:00:39,949
stays on duty.

25
00:00:39,949 --> 00:00:41,837
And here is the giveaway.

26
00:00:41,837 --> 00:00:43,349
A sleeping dolphin

27
00:00:43,349 --> 00:00:44,599
keeps one eye open.

28
00:00:44,599 --> 00:00:46,536
The eye on the opposite side

29
00:00:46,536 --> 00:00:47,649
of the sleeping half

30
00:00:47,649 --> 00:00:49,224
watching for predators.

31
00:00:50,126 --> 00:00:51,638
They drift near the surface

32
00:00:51,638 --> 00:00:52,901
resting motionless

33
00:00:52,901 --> 00:00:53,963
or swimming slowly

34
00:00:53,963 --> 00:00:55,513
and rise every few minutes

35
00:00:55,513 --> 00:00:57,100
for a calm, easy breath.

36
00:00:57,100 --> 00:00:58,525
Over a full day

37
00:00:58,525 --> 00:00:59,838
each half of the brain

38
00:00:59,838 --> 00:01:01,625
gets about four hours of sleep.

39
00:01:02,501 --> 00:01:04,638
New mothers do not get that luxury.

40
00:01:04,638 --> 00:01:05,875
For a whole month

41
00:01:05,875 --> 00:01:07,063
after a calf is born

42
00:01:07,063 --> 00:01:08,175
mother and baby

43
00:01:08,175 --> 00:01:09,363
barely sleep at all.

44
00:01:10,270 --> 00:01:11,594
Half a brain asleep.

45
00:01:11,594 --> 00:01:12,969
One eye open.

46
00:01:12,969 --> 00:01:14,507
And still breathing.

47
00:01:14,507 --> 00:01:16,595
That is how a dolphin sleeps

48
00:01:16,595 --> 00:01:17,557
without drowning.
